[00:15.93]Hello darkness, my old friend,
[00:23.95]I've come to talk with you again,
[00:32.22]Because a vision softly creeping,
[00:39.99]Left its seeds while I was sleeping,
[00:48.33]And the vision that was planted in my brain,
[00:58.21]Still remains,
[01:03.95]Within the sound of silence.
[01:13.43]In restless dreams I walked alone,
[01:21.05]Narrow streets of cobblestone,
[01:28.94]Beneath the halo of a street lamp,
[01:36.65]I turned my collar to the cold and damp,
[01:44.82]When my eyes were stabbed by the flash of a neon light,
[01:54.89]That split the night,
[02:00.67]And touched the sound of silence.
[02:09.68]And in the naked light I saw,
[02:17.38]Ten thousand people, maybe more,
[02:25.59]People talking without speaking,
[02:33.72]People hearing without listening,
[02:41.51]People writing songs that voices never share,
[02:51.35]And no one dare,
[02:57.14]Disturb the sound of silence.
[03:05.10]"Fools" said I, "You do not know,
[03:13.78]Silence like a cancer grows,
[03:21.57]Hear my words that I might teach you,
[03:29.62]Take my arms that I might reach you,"
[03:37.38]But my words, like silent raindrops fell,
[03:47.30]And echoed in the wells of silence.
[03:59.62]And the people bowed and prayed,
[04:09.13]To the neon god they made,
[04:16.89]And the sign flashed out its warning,
[04:24.47]In the words that it was forming,
[04:32.42]And the sign said "The words on the prophets are writ on the subway walls,
[04:43.76]And tenement halls,
[04:49.03]And whispered in the sound,
[04:59.04]Of silence."
